Question: What steps would you take to identify any issues in the code?
The first thing I would do is check the declarations and make sure every variable is spelled the same way everywhere it shows up. After that, I would walk trhough the program one line at a  time using sample numbers, like 100 and 80, and see if the results match what I expect. Doing that, I found a few problems: there is no input for 
firstTest before the loop or at the end of it, ouput is misspelled, and firstTest + secondTest /2 only divides secondTest by 2 because of the order of operations.
Question: What actions could the developer have taken to minimize the number of errors?
The devloper could have tested the program with sample values while writing it instead of waiting until the end. Reading back through the pseudocode, using consistent names, and having someone else look it over would have caught the typos and missing input statements early on.

